  "alerts": [
    {
      "item": "lem-sr-proper-time-reparametrization-invariance",
      "finding": "Facts [L7] says that the future and past timelike sets 'both are closed under multiplication by positive, respectively negative, scalars'. Read literally, this asserts closure of C− under negative scaling, which is false: v=-e0∈C− gives (-1)v=e0∈C+. The formulas immediately following correctly state positive scaling of a future vector and negative scaling of a future vector into C−; Proof 3.2 also uses that correct rule. The prose clause misstates the cited cone proposition.",
      "severity": "presentation"
    }
  ],
